# Personal-default overrides — author-specific values that the runtime layer reads
# from %LocalAppData%\TargetPlanner\personal-defaults.json. The committed source
# only ships ship-safe placeholders; this defensive gate stops a stray copy from
# ever ending up in the repo.
personal-defaults.json

# Claude Code harness state (per-developer permission allowlist, scheduled-task locks).
# Recreated by the harness; not project-relevant.
.claude/

# Local snapshot of the user's Target Scheduler database — kept for schema/data
# reference when designing IS/ISP/XisfManager work; ~100+ MB and contains personal
# imaging history, do not commit. Markdown docs co-located with the snapshot
# (e.g. TS_SCHEDULER_INGEST.md, which documents the schema the snapshot embodies)
# are tracked via the negation rule below. NOTE: gitignore can't re-include
# files whose PARENT directory is excluded -- so we ignore the directory's
# CONTENTS (TS DataBase Example/*) rather than the directory itself, then
# re-include .md siblings. Don't replace this with `TS DataBase Example/` or
# the negation silently stops working.
TS DataBase Example/*
!TS DataBase Example/*.md

